  "result": "Perfect! All 132 tests pass. I've successfully added payment tracking:\n\n**New error codes in `src/errors.js`:**\n- `NOT_ISSUED` \u2014 Can only record payments on issued or partially paid invoices\n- `OVERPAYMENT` \u2014 Payment exceeds the amount still owed\n\n**New file `src/payments.js` with two functions:**\n\n1. **`recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`** \u2014 Records a payment:\n   - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with payment added to `invoice.payments` array\n   - Validates status is 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (error NOT_ISSUED)\n   - Validates amount is a positive integer (error AMOUNT_INVALID)\n   - Checks payment doesn't exceed balance due (error OVERPAYMENT)\n   - Updates status to 'paid' when fully paid, 'partially_paid' otherwise\n   - Never mutates the input invoice\n\n2. **`balanceDue(invoice)`** \u2014 Calculates the amount still owed:\n   - Returns invoice total minus all recorded payments\n   - Returns 0 if fully paid\n   - Handles invoices with no payments or missing payments array\n\n**Tests (16 payment tests added):**\n- Balance due calculations (issued invoices, with discounts, with VAT)\n- Partial payment recording\n- Full payment setting status to 'paid'\n- Status change to 'partially_paid' for partial payments\n- Rejection of payments on draft/paid invoices\n- Amount validation (integer, positive, no overpayments)\n- Multiple payments on single invoice\n- Non-mutation of original invoices\n- Correct balance calculation after payments\n\nThe payment system integrates seamlessly with invoices, properly calculating totals that include discounts and VAT.",
